Syntax: trap <arrow> <trap type>      (e.g. "trap arrow fire")

Set Arrow Trap allows a skilled thief to rig an arrow with a concealed trap.
The arrow must be carried out of any quiver, and is consumed when setting the
trap.  The trap type is always the last word of the command.

When the rigged arrow finds its mark, the trap is delivered to the victim,
potentially causing significant damage. The quality of the arrow affects the
damage dealt, and poisoned arrows retain their venom.

More skilled trappers can set deadlier traps that are harder to detect and
more likely to strike true. Failed attempts may trigger the trap prematurely,
potentially injuring the trapper themselves.

Class: Thief
Discipline: Traps

